if (cfg->fc_flags & RTF_REJECT) {
```
Reason:
The fix replaces the overly broad `fib6_is_reject()` check with a direct check of the `RTF_REJECT` flag. Only explicit reject routes (which set `RTF_REJECT`) will skip `fib_nh_common_init()`. Standalone nexthop objects and implicit loopback routes (which do not have `RTF_REJECT`) now take the normal initialization path, ensuring `nhc_pcpu_rth_output` is properly allocated. This prevents the NULL pointer dereference when IPv4 routes reference such nexthops.

